You are extracting structured data from scanned MOCNESS tow datasheets.

INPUTS:
- One or two images are provided for a tow.
- Form image name pattern: tow_<ID>_form.png
- Optional notes image name pattern: tow_<ID>_notes.png

GENERAL RULES:
- Return JSON only.
- If a field is unreadable or absent, return null.
- Preserve latitude/longitude exactly as written (no decimal conversion).
- Normalize times to HH:MM (24h) when readable.
- Keep local and GMT time fields separately.
- If a row time cell contains two times (stacked or slash-separated) and row-level mapping is ambiguous, set row time fields to null rather than guessing.
- If the form has separate `GMT Date` and `Local Date` fields, extract both into `gmt_date` and `local_date`.
  - If both are present and identical, also set `date` to that value and `date_unresolved=false`.
  - If both are present and differ, set `date` to null, `date_unresolved=true`, and explain the conflict in `date_unresolved_reason`.
  - If only one is present, set `date` to that value.
- If the form has only a single `Date` field, set `date` from it and leave `local_date` and `gmt_date` as null.
- If date cannot be confidently resolved, set date to null and set date_unresolved=true with a reason.
- Net rows: keep only rows where net_number is explicit; if net_number is missing, exclude that row.
- Do not infer net_number from row order.
- Notes merge behavior per net:
	- notes_table: notes written in the NET TOW table row.
	- notes_notes_page: notes from notes page matched by net number (usually just numeric net labels).
	- notes: if both exist, concatenate as "<notes_table>; <notes_notes_page>".
	- Keep exact text; duplicates are allowed.
- Interpret slashed-zero symbols as numeric/text zero where applicable.

FORM VARIANTS TO HANDLE:
- Header fields can include:
	Cruise, Tow/Moc#, Date, Location, D/N, Direction, Sea State, Wind Speed,
	Local Time (from/to), GMT Time (from/to), Net Condition, Net Mesh, Net Size,
	Start Lat, Start Long, End Lat, End Long.
- Some forms also include File Name, Type (net type), SOG, Operator.
- Coordinates may appear as Start Lat Long / End Lat Long; split into
	start_lat/start_long and end_lat/end_long when possible.
- NET TOW table columns vary; include all observed row values into canonical keys.
- Do not populate `depth_m` unless a distinct `Depth (m)` column is actually present on that form variant.
- If the form only has `Depth max (m)` and `Depth min (m)`, set `depth_m` to null for all rows.

OUTPUT SCHEMA (exact keys, no extras):
{
	"tow_id": "string",
	"header": {
		"cruise": "string|null",
		"tow_moc_number": "string|null",
		"file_name": "string|null",
		"date": "yyyy-mm-dd|string|null",
		"local_date": "yyyy-mm-dd|string|null",
		"gmt_date": "yyyy-mm-dd|string|null",
		"date_unresolved": "boolean|null",
		"date_unresolved_reason": "string|null",
		"location": "string|null",
		"day_night": "string|null",
		"direction": "string|null",
		"sea_state": "string|null",
		"wind_speed": "string|null",
		"local_time_from": "HH:MM|null",
		"local_time_to": "HH:MM|null",
		"gmt_time_from": "HH:MM|null",
		"gmt_time_to": "HH:MM|null",
		"net_condition": "string|null",
		"net_mesh": "string|null",
		"net_size": "string|null",
		"net_type": "string|null",
		"sog": "string|null",
		"operator": "string|null",
		"start_lat": "string|null",
		"start_long": "string|null",
		"end_lat": "string|null",
		"end_long": "string|null"
	},
	"form_comments": "string|null",
	"net_tows": [
		{
			"net_number": "string",
			"time_open_local": "HH:MM|null",
			"time_close_local": "HH:MM|null",
			"time_close_gmt": "HH:MM|null",
			"target_depth_m": "string|number|null",
			"depth_max_m": "string|number|null",
			"depth_min_m": "string|number|null",
			"depth_m": "string|number|null",
			"lat": "string|null",
			"lon": "string|null",
			"angle": "string|number|null",
			"flow_counts": "string|number|null",
			"volume_filtered": "string|number|null",
			"mwo_net": "string|null",
			"winch_speed": "string|number|null",
			"notes_table": "string|null",
			"notes_notes_page": "string|null",
			"notes": "string|null"
		}
	],
	"quality": {
		"field_confidence": {
			"field.path": "number from 0.0 to 1.0"
		},
		"uncertain_fields": ["field.path"],
		"notes": ["string"]
	}
}